# Names-only template. Uncomment and populate only the entries needed for this workflow.
# No defaults or credential values are provided. Optional unset variables retain code defaults.
# Names-only template. Uncomment and populate only the entries needed for this workflow.
# No defaults or credential values are provided. Optional unset variables retain code defaults.
# SECONDARY — GCP (Cloud Run), RPC provider B, keeper address B
# Copy to secondary.env (git-ignored). On Cloud Run, inject RPC_URLS and ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL
# from Secret Manager.

# KEEPER_INSTANCE=
# KEEPER_CONFIG=
# Comma-separated, first is preferred. Use a different provider than the primary.
# RPC_URLS=

# SIGNER=
# Algorithm EC_SIGN_SECP256K1_SHA256. The service account needs
# cloudkms.cryptoKeyVersions.viewPublicKey and cloudkms.cryptoKeyVersions.useToSign.
# GCP_KMS_KEY_NAME=
# GCP credentials: on Cloud Run they come from the service account — do not set keys here.
# Locally, run `gcloud auth application-default login`.

# Slack- or Discord-compatible webhook; empty disables alerts (they are still logged).
# ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Serves /healthz in `run` mode; omit for `once` (scheduled) deployments.
# PORT=
# debug | info | warn | error
# LOG_LEVEL=
# Optional: limit to a subset of jobs, e.g. JOBS=W5,W6. Unset runs all enabled jobs.
# JOBS=
